<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8"/>
    <meta content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" name="viewport"/>
    <title>The-Frame TV - Help &amp; Instructions</title>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600;700;800&amp;family=Orbitron:wght@600;700;900&amp;display=swap" rel="stylesheet"/>
    <style>
        /* =====================================================
           Scoped under .help-page so styles never leak into
           the host page when injected into #sub-content-overlay.
           ===================================================== */
        .help-page {
            --accent: #ffa260;
            --accent-bright: #ffbe8e;
            --gold: #daa520;
            --gold-light: #ffd700;
            --bg-dark: #07070a;
            --panel: rgba(18, 18, 24, 0.88);
            --card-bg: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
            --border-subtle: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
            --border-accent: rgba(255, 162, 96, 0.35);
            --text: #f5f5f7;
            --text-muted: #c8c8d0;
            --text-dim: #9494a0;
            --danger: #ff6b6b;
            --success: #2ecc71;
            --font-display: 'Orbitron', sans-serif;
            --font-body: 'Inter', sans-serif;

            position: fixed;
            inset: 0;
            overflow-x: hidden;
            overflow-y: auto;
            color: var(--text);
            font-family: var(--font-body);
            line-height: 1.65;
            background: radial-gradient(circle at top right, rgba(45, 30, 20, 0.65), rgba(5, 5, 8, 0.96));
            backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
            scrollbar-width: thin;
            scrollbar-color: var(--accent) var(--bg-dark);
            width: min(1100px, calc(100% - 2rem));
            margin: 2rem auto 0;
            border-radius: 16px 16px 0 0;
            border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
            box-shadow: 0 20px 60px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.75);
        }

        .help-page * {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        /* ---------- Custom Scrollbar ---------- */
        .help-page::-webkit-scrollbar { width: 10px; }
        .help-page::-webkit-scrollbar-track { background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4); }
        .help-page::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
            background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--accent) 0%, var(--gold) 100%);
            border-radius: 999px;
            border: 2px solid var(--bg-dark);
        }
        .help-page::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover { background: var(--accent-bright); }

        .help-page .container {
            max-width: 1020px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 2rem 2.5rem 3rem;
        }

        /* ---------- Floating Top Bar & Back Button ---------- */
        .help-page .top-nav {
            position: sticky;
            top: 0;
            z-index: 100;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            align-items: center;
            padding: 1rem 2.5rem;
            background: rgba(10, 10, 14, 0.85);
            backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
        }

        .help-page .nav-brand {
            font-family: var(--font-display);
            font-size: 0.95rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            letter-spacing: 1.5px;
            color: var(--text);
        }
        .help-page .nav-brand span { color: var(--accent); }

        .help-page .back-btn {
            display: inline-flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 0.5rem;
            padding: 0.45rem 1.2rem;
            background: rgba(255, 162, 96, 0.12);
            color: var(--accent);
            border: 1px solid var(--border-accent);
            border-radius: 999px;
            font-family: var(--font-display);
            font-size: 0.8rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            letter-spacing: 1px;
            text-decoration: none;
            cursor: pointer;
            transition: all 0.2s ease;
        }

        .help-page a:focus-visible,
        .help-page button:focus-visible {
            outline: 2px solid var(--accent-bright);
            outline-offset: 3px;
        }

        .help-page .back-btn:hover,
        .help-page .back-btn:focus-visible {
            background: var(--accent);
            color: #000;
            box-shadow: 0 0 18px rgba(255, 162, 96, 0.45);
            outline: none;
        }

        /* ---------- Hero Header ---------- */
        .help-page .header {
            text-align: center;
            padding: 2.5rem 2rem;
            margin-bottom: 2rem;
            background: linear-gradient(145deg, rgba(255, 162, 96, 0.08) 0%, rgba(15, 15, 20, 0.7) 100%);
            border: 1px solid var(--border-accent);
            border-radius: 16px;
        }

        .help-page .version-pill {
            display: inline-block;
            padding: 0.25rem 0.9rem;
            margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
            background: rgba(46, 204, 113, 0.15);
            color: var(--success);
            border: 1px solid rgba(46, 204, 113, 0.35);
            border-radius: 999px;
            font-size: 0.75rem;
            font-weight: 600;
            letter-spacing: 1px;
            text-transform: uppercase;
        }

        .help-page h1 {
            font-family: var(--font-display);
            font-size: 2.6rem;
            font-weight: 900;
            letter-spacing: 2px;
            margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ffffff 0%, var(--accent) 60%, var(--gold-light) 100%);
            -webkit-background-clip: text;
            background-clip: text;
            -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
        }

        .help-page .subtitle {
            color: var(--text-muted);
            font-size: 1rem;
            font-weight: 400;
        }

        /* ---------- Sections ---------- */
        .help-page .section {
            scroll-margin-top: 6rem;
            background: var(--panel);
            border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
            border-radius: 16px;
            padding: 2rem;
            margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
            transition: border-color 0.25s ease;
        }

        .help-page .section:hover {
            border-color: var(--border-accent);
        }

        .help-page h2 {
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 0.75rem;
            font-family: var(--font-display);
            font-size: 1.35rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            letter-spacing: 1px;
            color: var(--accent);
            padding-bottom: 0.85rem;
            margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
            border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 162, 96, 0.25);
            text-transform: uppercase;
        }

        .help-page h3 {
            font-family: var(--font-display);
            font-size: 1.05rem;
            color: var(--gold-light);
            margin: 1.4rem 0 0.65rem;
            letter-spacing: 0.5px;
        }

        .help-page h4 {
            font-family: var(--font-display);
            font-size: 0.95rem;
            color: var(--accent-bright);
            margin: 1rem 0 0.35rem;
            letter-spacing: 0.4px;
        }

        .help-page p {
            color: var(--text-muted);
            font-size: 0.95rem;
            margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
        }

        .help-page ul {
            list-style: none;
            margin: 0.6rem 0 1rem 0.5rem;
        }

        .help-page ul li {
            position: relative;
            padding-left: 1.25rem;
            margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
            color: var(--text-muted);
            font-size: 0.92rem;
        }

        .help-page ul li::before {
            content: "•";
            position: absolute;
            left: 0;
            color: var(--accent);
            font-weight: bold;
        }

        /* ---------- Step Lists ---------- */
        .help-page .step-list {
            list-style: none;
            counter-reset: step-counter;
            margin: 1.25rem 0;
        }

        .help-page .step-list li {
            counter-increment: step-counter;
            position: relative;
            margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
            padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem 0.9rem 3.4rem;
            background: var(--card-bg);
            border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
            border-radius: 10px;
            color: var(--text-muted);
            font-size: 0.92rem;
            line-height: 1.6;
        }

        .help-page .step-list li::before {
            content: counter(step-counter);
            position: absolute;
            left: 1rem;
            top: 1rem;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            width: 1.75rem;
            height: 1.75rem;
            border-radius: 50%;
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent) 0%, var(--gold) 100%);
            color: #000;
            font-family: var(--font-display);
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            font-weight: 800;
        }

        .help-page .step-list li > strong:first-child {
            display: block;
            color: var(--text);
            font-size: 1rem;
            margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
        }

        .help-page .step-list li strong {
            display: inline;
            color: var(--accent-bright);
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        .help-page .step-list li ul {
            margin: 0.45rem 0 0 0;
        }

        .help-page .step-list li ul li {
            counter-increment: none;
            background: transparent;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 0;
            padding: 0 0 0 1.15rem;
            margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
            font-size: 0.9rem;
        }

        .help-page .step-list li ul li::before {
            content: "•";
            position: absolute;
            left: 0;
            top: 0;
            width: auto;
            height: auto;
            background: none;
            color: var(--accent);
            font-family: var(--font-body);
            font-size: 0.95rem;
            font-weight: bold;
        }

        /* ---------- Feature Grid ---------- */
        .help-page .feature-grid {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(270px, 1fr));
            gap: 1.15rem;
            margin-top: 1.25rem;
        }

        .help-page .feature-card {
            background: var(--card-bg);
            border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
            border-radius: 12px;
            padding: 1.25rem;
            min-width: 0;
            transition: all 0.25s ease;
        }

        .help-page .feature-card:hover {
            border-color: var(--accent);
            background: rgba(255, 162, 96, 0.05);
            transform: translateY(-2px);
        }

        .help-page .feature-card h4 {
            font-family: var(--font-display);
            font-size: 0.95rem;
            color: var(--accent-bright);
            margin: 0 0 0.45rem 0;
            letter-spacing: 0.5px;
        }

        .help-page .feature-card p {
            font-size: 0.86rem;
            color: var(--text-dim);
            margin: 0;
            line-height: 1.55;
        }

        /* ---------- Callout Boxes ---------- */
        .help-page .tip-box {
            background: rgba(255, 162, 96, 0.08);
            border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
            border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
            padding: 1rem 1.35rem;
            margin: 1.25rem 0;
            font-size: 0.9rem;
            color: var(--text-muted);
        }

        .help-page .tip-box strong { color: var(--accent-bright); }

        .help-page .warning-box {
            background: rgba(255, 107, 107, 0.09);
            border-left: 4px solid var(--danger);
            border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
            padding: 1rem 1.35rem;
            margin: 1.25rem 0;
            font-size: 0.9rem;
            color: #ffcccc;
        }

        .help-page .warning-box strong { color: #ff8787; }

        /* ---------- Code / Notecard Block ---------- */
        .help-page .code-block {
            background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
            border: 1px solid rgba(255, 162, 96, 0.25);
            border-radius: 8px;
            padding: 0.9rem 1.15rem;
            margin: 0.85rem 0;
            font-family: monospace;
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            color: var(--gold-light);
            line-height: 1.5;
            overflow-wrap: anywhere;
        }

        /* ---------- FAQ / Troubleshooting ---------- */
        .help-page .faq-item {
            margin-bottom: 1.15rem;
            padding-bottom: 1.15rem;
            border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
        }

        .help-page .faq-item:last-child {
            margin-bottom: 0;
            padding-bottom: 0;
            border-bottom: none;
        }

        .help-page .faq-question {
            color: var(--accent-bright);
            font-weight: 600;
            font-size: 0.96rem;
            margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
        }

        .help-page .faq-answer {
            color: var(--text-dim);
            font-size: 0.9rem;
            padding-left: 1.1rem;
        }

        /* ---------- Badges ---------- */
        .help-page .badge-group {
            display: flex;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            gap: 0.5rem;
            margin: 0.75rem 0 1.25rem;
        }

        .help-page .badge {
            padding: 0.35rem 0.85rem;
            background: rgba(255, 162, 96, 0.1);
            color: var(--accent-bright);
            border: 1px solid rgba(255, 162, 96, 0.3);
            border-radius: 999px;
            font-size: 0.78rem;
            font-weight: 500;
        }

        /* ---------- Footer ---------- */
        .help-page .footer {
            text-align: center;
            padding: 1.75rem 1rem;
            margin-top: 1rem;
            background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45);
            border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
            border-radius: 14px;
        }

        .help-page .footer p {
            color: var(--text-dim);
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
        }

        .help-page .footer .creator {
            color: var(--accent);
            font-weight: 600;
            font-size: 0.95rem;
        }

        /* ---------- Responsive layout & accessibility ---------- */
        .help-page .toc {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(190px, 1fr));
            gap: 0.65rem;
            margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
            padding: 1.25rem;
            background: var(--panel);
            border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
            border-radius: 14px;
        }
        .help-page .toc-title {
            grid-column: 1 / -1;
            color: var(--accent-bright);
            font-family: var(--font-display);
            font-size: 0.9rem;
            letter-spacing: 1px;
            text-transform: uppercase;
        }
        .help-page .toc a {
            display: block;
            padding: 0.65rem 0.8rem;
            color: var(--text-muted);
            text-decoration: none;
            font-size: 0.86rem;
            border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
            border-radius: 8px;
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.025);
            transition: border-color 0.2s ease, color 0.2s ease, background 0.2s ease;
        }
        .help-page .toc a:hover {
            color: var(--accent-bright);
            border-color: var(--border-accent);
            background: rgba(255, 162, 96, 0.06);
        }
        .help-page .section p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

        @media (max-width: 700px) {
            .help-page {
                width: 100%;
                margin: 0;
                border-radius: 0;
                border-left: 0;
                border-right: 0;
            }
            .help-page .top-nav {
                padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
                gap: 0.75rem;
            }
            .help-page .nav-brand {
                font-size: 0.72rem;
                letter-spacing: 0.8px;
            }
            .help-page .back-btn {
                padding: 0.4rem 0.75rem;
                font-size: 0.68rem;
                white-space: nowrap;
            }
            .help-page .container {
                padding: 1rem 1rem 2rem;
            }
            .help-page .header {
                padding: 1.75rem 1rem;
                margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
            }
            .help-page h1 { font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 8vw, 2.3rem); }
            .help-page .subtitle { font-size: 0.9rem; }
            .help-page .section {
                padding: 1.2rem;
                margin-bottom: 1rem;
            }
            .help-page h2 {
                font-size: 1rem;
                line-height: 1.45;
            }
            .help-page .step-list li {
                padding: 0.85rem 0.85rem 0.85rem 3rem;
            }
            .help-page .feature-grid {
                grid-template-columns: 1fr;
            }
            .help-page .toc {
                grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
                padding: 1rem;
            }
        }
        @media (max-width: 380px) {
            .help-page .toc { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
            .help-page .nav-brand { max-width: 55%; }
        }
        @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
            .help-page *,
            .help-page *::before,
            .help-page *::after {
                scroll-behavior: auto !important;
                transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
                animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="help-page">
    <!-- Sticky Navigation Bar -->
    <div class="top-nav">
        <div class="nav-brand">THE-FRAME TV <span>// USER GUIDE</span></div>
        <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; align-items: center;">
            <a aria-label="Back to top" class="back-btn" href="#" id="topBtn">TOP &uarr;</a>
            <a aria-label="Go back" class="back-btn" href="#" id="backBtn">&larr; BACK TO MENU</a>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="container">
        <!-- Hero Header -->
        <header class="header">
            <div class="version-pill">Premium Edition V4.1 &bull; Full Access</div>
            <h1>📺 THE-FRAME TV</h1>
            <p class="subtitle">Looks, Feels, and Works Like a Real TV — Complete Setup &amp; User Manual</p>
        </header>

        <!-- Quick Navigation -->
        <nav aria-label="Manual contents" class="toc">
            <div class="toc-title">Quick Navigation</div>
            <a href="#viewer-preferences">1. Viewer Preferences</a>
            <a href="#power-navigation">2. Power &amp; Controls</a>
            <a href="#main-menu">3. Main Menu &amp; Apps</a>
            <a href="#shared-sync">4. Shared Sync, Kosmi &amp; CyTube</a>
            <a href="#slideshows">5. Picture Slideshows</a>
            <a href="#setup-workflow">6. TV Setup &amp; Settings</a>
            <a href="#troubleshooting">7. Troubleshooting</a>
            <a href="#tech-specs">8. Tech Specs</a>
            <a href="#disclaimer">9. Disclaimer</a>
        </nav>

        <div class="tip-box" role="note">
            <strong>How to use this guide:</strong> Start with Viewer Media Preferences, then follow the sections in order. If you need help with a specific feature, use Quick Navigation to jump directly to that section.
        </div>

        <!-- 1. VIEWER PREFERENCES -->
        <section class="section" id="viewer-preferences">
            <h2><span>⚠️</span> 1. Viewer Media Preferences</h2>
            <p>Before powering on your TV, ensure your Second Life viewer is configured to play shared media properly. In <strong>Firestorm</strong> (or your preferred viewer), navigate to <strong>Preferences &rarr; Sound &amp; Media &rarr; Media</strong> and verify:</p>
            <ol class="step-list">
                <li><strong>Toggle Media Auto-Play to ENABLE</strong>Ensures streams and menus launch automatically when powered on.</li>
                <li><strong>Check "Allow Inworld Scripts to Play Media"</strong>Required for the TV's LSL handshake and screen synchronization.</li>
                <li><strong>Check "Play Media Attached to Other Avatars"</strong>Ensures full compatibility across shared media surfaces and rooms.</li>
            </ol>
        </section>

        <!-- 2. POWERING ON & NAVIGATION -->
        <section class="section" id="power-navigation">
            <h2><span>📺</span> 2. Powering On &amp; Basic Controls</h2>
            <p>Click the <strong>TV Power button</strong> to establish a secure connection with the server. Within a few seconds, the Main Menu featuring all 12 entertainment apps will appear on screen.</p>

            <div class="tip-box">
                <strong>💡 Quick Navigation Tips:</strong><br/>
                &bull; <strong>Back Button:</strong> When watching a video, click anywhere on the screen or top edge to reveal a Back/Sync button.<br/>
                &bull; <strong>Close Pages:</strong> Look for the <strong>&times;</strong> icon in the top corners to exit apps or settings.<br/>
                &bull; <strong>Top Bar:</strong> On several views, check the top row for extra search, room, or wallpaper options.
            </div>

            <div class="warning-box">
                <strong>⚠️ Menu Fails to Load in 30 Seconds?</strong><br/>
                Double-check your viewer media preferences above, verify you can play media on other devices, or try rezzing the TV on another parcel/sandbox. For personal assistance, send an in-world notecard to <strong>pedrosilva2014</strong>.
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 3. SURFING THE MAIN MENU -->
        <section class="section" id="main-menu">
            <h2><span>✨</span> 3. Main Menu &amp; Entertainment Apps</h2>
            <p>Powered by real-time Socket.IO synchronization, everyone connected to your TV room experiences the exact same playback and game states simultaneously.</p>

            <div class="feature-grid">
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>📺 YouTube</h4>
                    <p>Ad-free video player. Search any keyword, paste direct links, enter a Channel ID, or browse our curated playlists.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>🎵 Music</h4>
                    <p>Curated selection of YouTube music channels and mixes—ideal for background ambiance, parties, and venues.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>🎬 Movies</h4>
                    <p>Browse selected YouTube movie channels for synchronized movie nights. (We do not host or stream copyrighted movies).</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>📻 Radios</h4>
                    <p>Live global Shoutcast &amp; Icecast radio streams, proxied through our server to prevent HTTPS mixed-content drops.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>🔒 XXX (Protected)</h4>
                    <p>Adult content section protected by password. The default access password is <strong>slxxx</strong>.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>🗺️ Second Life</h4>
                    <p>Explore the SL Destination Guide with photo previews and direct teleport SLURL buttons to visit featured lands.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>🎮 Games</h4>
                    <p>Ad-free casual clip games and real-time socket multiplayer games (Quiz Trivia, True/Myth, Chess, and more) to play with friends.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>🎁 Freebies</h4>
                    <p>Up-to-date directory of Second Life freebies, hunts, and active store gifts.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>📸 Flickr &amp; Slideshows</h4>
                    <p>Explore Flickr tags/groups, set photos as TV background wallpapers, or launch photo slideshows.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>🤝 Party Share</h4>
                    <p>Create and share synchronized rooms with friends, duplicate TV screens, or launch Kosmi &amp; CyTube watch parties.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>🌐 Browsers</h4>
                    <p>Curated links to popular web pages. <em>Tip: Enable the Nav Bar in Security settings first to get a browser Back button.</em></p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>🎥 Live TV &amp; WebRTC</h4>
                    <p>Watch live streams or share your own screen/gameplay with ultra-low latency WebRTC peer-to-peer streaming.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="tip-box">
                <strong>💡 Party Share Tip:</strong> Explore the Party Share app in the main menu to connect with friends and host collaborative watch sessions!
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 4. SHARED SYNC VIEW, KOSMI & CYTUBE -->
        <section class="section" id="shared-sync">
            <h2><span>🤝</span> 4. Shared Sync View, Kosmi &amp; CyTube</h2>
            <p>The-Frame TV is built for social environments and group entertainment. Through Party Share and real-time Socket.IO synchronization, you can effortlessly host watch parties.</p>

            <h3>Built-in Real-Time Synchronization</h3>
            <p>Party Share provides options for watching with other people. The built-in system synchronizes playback for viewers connected to the same TV room, ensuring everyone sees identical video and game states simultaneously.</p>

            <div class="tip-box">
                <strong>💡 Shared Viewing Etiquette:</strong> When using a shared room, playback and game-state changes are visible to all connected viewers. Use a separate private room when you want an uninterrupted session.
            </div>

            <h3>External Watch Parties (Kosmi &amp; CyTube)</h3>
            <p>In addition to the built-in sync engine, you can launch external watch parties directly from Party Share:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Kosmi Integration:</strong> Host virtual rooms with synchronized video playback, voice chat, and web browsing.</li>
                <li><strong>CyTube Rooms:</strong> Queue media playlists and enjoy synchronized multi-user chat and broadcasting.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Sharing the TV with Others in Venues</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Always ask before changing videos or channels if other guests are actively watching.</li>
                <li>Choose media appropriate for the parcel's theme and audience.</li>
                <li>If control is restricted, the parcel owner may have limited playback toggles exclusively to staff or owners.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- 5. SL PICTURES SLIDESHOW (NATIVE & CUSTOM NOTECARD) -->
        <section class="section" id="slideshows">
            <h2><span>🖼️</span> 5. Picture Slideshows (Native &amp; Custom Notecard)</h2>
            <p>In addition to Flickr browsing, your TV includes a dedicated Picture Slideshow mode supporting both built-in galleries and your own personal Second Life textures.</p>

            <h3>A. Native TV Slideshow</h3>
            <p>Open the Slideshow view from the menu to play a curated gallery of high-resolution visuals automatically. Use the on-screen controls to pause, skip forward/backward, or adjust the transition interval between slides.</p>

            <h3>B. Custom Notecard Slideshow</h3>
            <p>Display your own Second Life snapshots, store banners, or artwork by creating a custom slideshow notecard:</p>
            <ol class="step-list">
                <li><strong>Create a New Notecard</strong>In your Second Life inventory, create a new notecard (e.g., <em>My Slideshow</em>).</li>
                <li><strong>Paste Your Texture UUIDs</strong>Right-click your full-perm textures in inventory, select <em>Copy Asset UUID</em>, and paste one UUID per line inside the notecard, then click <strong>Save</strong>.</li>
                <li><strong>Drop Into the TV Contents</strong>Right-click the TV in-world &rarr; <strong>Edit</strong> &rarr; open the <strong>Contents</strong> tab, and drag your saved notecard inside. Select your notecard in the TV Slideshow menu to start displaying your custom album!</li>
            </ol>
            <div class="code-block">
                Example Notecard Format (one UUID per line):<br/>
                369104f6-cb0e-4920-a41a-ac2f8c42337e<br/>
                21d7c8a9-28c5-f436-083d-2b7d0d594dec<br/>
                704acfcc-dade-771a-c943-c295b464e2d9
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 6. ON-SCREEN SETTINGS & SETUP WORKFLOW -->
        <section class="section" id="setup-workflow">
            <h2><span>🛠️</span> 6. Step-by-Step TV Setup &amp; Settings Flow</h2>
            <p>Click the <strong>Settings / Gear button</strong> at the bottom of the Main Menu to open the configuration panel. Follow the steps in order to tailor your TV to your space:</p>

            <ol class="step-list">
                <li>
                    <strong>Unlock Settings (If Protected)</strong>
                    If password protection is active, enter the server settings password listed in your info notecard. <em>(If entered incorrectly, an Access Denied prompt will remind you to check your notecard).</em>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Step 1 — Design &amp; Style (Hardware Look)</strong>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Stand Model:</strong> Choose between Model 1, Model 2, or Model 3.</li>
                        <li><strong>TV Texture:</strong> Apply Carbon Fiber, Wood, Grey Stone, Dark Grey, Passerele, or Ivory White.</li>
                        <li><strong>Mount Mode:</strong> Switch between Stand or Wall mount.</li>
                        <li><strong>Back Color &amp; Alpha:</strong> Pick a back panel color and fine-tune Back / Webscreen transparency (0%&ndash;20%).</li>
                        <li><strong>Frame Mode:</strong> Toggle the outer bezel frame (Show / Hide).</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Step 2 — Shape &amp; Size (Dimensions &amp; Ratio)</strong>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Manual Scale:</strong> Resize the TV in precise steps from <strong>&minus;20% to +20%</strong>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Environment Presets:</strong> Apply one-click sizing for <strong>House</strong>, <strong>Outside</strong>, or <strong>Cinema</strong>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Aspect Ratios:</strong> Switch from 1:1 Square up to 16:9 Full HD, 21:9 Cinema Scope, or 32:9 Dual Ultrawide.</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Step 3 — Ambilight &amp; Neon (Lighting &amp; Mood)</strong>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Light &amp; Neon Mode:</strong> Set backlights and neon accents to <strong>Off</strong>, <strong>On</strong>, or <strong>Color Cycle</strong>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Mood Presets:</strong> Apply quick lighting profiles (<strong>Active</strong>, <strong>Normal</strong>, or <strong>Cozy</strong>).</li>
                        <li><strong>Fine Tuning:</strong> Customize glow color, cycle speed, intensity, range, falloff, and glow level.</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Step 4 — Security &amp; Alarm (Access &amp; Protection)</strong>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>House Alarm:</strong> Enable or disable the proximity security alarm.</li>
                        <li><strong>Sensor Range:</strong> Set detection radius in meters (<strong>1m&ndash;50m</strong>).</li>
                        <li><strong>Lock TV:</strong> Restrict power and playback controls exclusively to the owner.</li>
                        <li><strong>Navigation Bar:</strong> Show or hide the Second Life browser navigation bar.</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Step 5 — System Maintenance &amp; Resets</strong>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Default Settings / Factory Default:</strong> Restore original parameters (protected by a confirmation modal).</li>
                        <li><strong>Reset Scripts:</strong> Restart internal scripts to clear lag or refresh state.</li>
                        <li><strong>Password Protection:</strong> Toggle the settings access password on or off.</li>
                        <li><strong>Delete TV:</strong> Safely remove the TV object from your parcel (with confirmation prompt).</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
            </ol>

            <div class="warning-box">
                <strong>⚠️ Active Connection Required:</strong> On-screen settings require an active connection between the TV and the server. If controls become unresponsive, turn the TV <strong>Off and On again</strong> to reconnect.
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 7. TROUBLESHOOTING & FAQ -->
        <section class="section" id="troubleshooting">
            <h2><span>🔧</span> 7. Troubleshooting &amp; FAQ</h2>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">⬛ TV Screen is Black or Menu Won't Load</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">Ensure <strong>"Allow Inworld Scripts to Play Media"</strong> is checked in Viewer Preferences and that pop-ups are not blocked for the TV's page. Right-click the TV prim and select <strong>Play</strong>, or toggle the TV power button off and on.</div>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">🔊 No Sound or Audio Drops</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">Unmute media in the top-right corner of your viewer toolbar and verify your system volume. Our Node.js server automatically proxies streams to prevent HTTPS mixed-content drops.</div>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">⚡ Out of Sync with Other Viewers</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">Click the top edge of the TV screen and hit <strong>Back</strong> or <strong>Sync</strong> to realign your Socket.IO room session. Also verify that everyone is connected to the same TV room.</div>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">🌐 Browser Page Does Not Load</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">Some viewers enforce stricter media security rules. If your viewer uses a media or URL whitelist, ensure the TV's page is allowed.</div>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">🎬 Audio Plays, But Video Picture is Missing</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">Reopen the app or toggle the TV Power button off and on to refresh the stream. If the issue persists, the original third-party source may have been removed or is temporarily offline.</div>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">🐢 Video Playback is Laggy</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">Lower your viewer's graphics settings or move closer to the TV. While the TV interface runs at <strong>1280&times;720</strong>, external HD streams may require additional bandwidth or GPU resources.</div>
            </div>
        </section>

